    "text": "A bottle has an opening of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math>. A cork of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, is compressed to fit into the opening completely (see figure). If the bulk modulus of cork is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and the coefficient of friction between the bottle and cork is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></math>, then the force needed to push the cork into the bottle is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/135530.JPG\" style=\"width: 75px; height: 177px;\" />",
